course: dictionary
lesson: 15379
title: Speakerphone and phone words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A speakerphone is a phone setting that plays the caller's voice through a loudspeaker. Everyone in the room can hear and talk, and nobody has to hold the phone. «Mum put Grandma on speakerphone so we could all say hello.» Here on speakerphone means the call is played out loud for the whole room.
explain: Look at the two parts of the word: speaker, which makes sound louder, and phone, which you use to call people. Put them together and you get a phone that speaks out loud. «The new speakerphone in the kitchen is very loud.» Here speakerphone is a device you can place on a table.
explain: Speakerphone can mean the setting or the device, so check the sentence. Try your meaning in it: «Switch to speakerphone» makes sense, so here it is a setting you turn on. Drivers use speakerphone or hands-free so they do not need to hold the phone. «Please use speakerphone in the car, and keep your eyes on the road.»
fact: A speakerphone is a setting on a phone, or a phone or device, that uses a loudspeaker.
fact: On speakerphone means the call is played out loud so everyone in the room can listen.
fact: «Put it on speakerphone» means switch the call to the loudspeaker.
fact: Speakerphone is a noun: «a speakerphone» and «speakerphones» are both correct.
fact: Safety tip: drivers use speakerphone or hands-free so they do not hold the phone, and you should tell the caller if others can hear.
exercise: «Mum put Grandma on speakerphone so everyone could say hello.» What does on speakerphone mean? | The call has ended | Grandma is sleeping | *The call is played out loud so the whole room can hear | The phone is hidden in a bag
exercise: «The new speakerphone sat in the middle of the table.» What is a speakerphone in this sentence? | *A phone device with a loudspeaker | A lamp | A kind of pencil case | A type of table
exercise: Why should a driver use speakerphone or hands-free? | So the car goes faster | So the phone is never lost | So they can watch videos | *So they do not have to hold the phone
test: Which word is made from speaker and phone? | speakerbox | *speakerphone | loudspace | phonebook
test: Complete the sentence: «Please switch to ___ so Dad can hear too.» | *speakerphone | calendar | carpet | television
exam: Ella says, «Tell Nan we are on speakerphone.» What should Nan know? | *Everyone in the room can hear her | Nan has to whisper | Ella is in the bath | The call has been cut off
